// Two derivations that differ only in a wildcard column (BENCH-135 "2 derivations"; the property of the
// repeated-firings-with-wildcards test in Molly's provenance suite, R06 §12.6), written for this corpus: `stock`
// records each shelf that holds an item, and `available` reads it with the shelf written as `_`, so available(n,
// "pen") has one derivation through stock(n, "s1", "pen") and one through stock(n, "s2", "pen"). Blossom golden
// corpus, re-derived (derived = true); see ../../README.md.

stock(N, Shelf, Item) :- shelved(N, Item, Shelf);
available(N, Item) :- wanted(N, Item), stock(N, _, Item);

shelved("n", "pen", "s1")@1;
shelved("n", "pen", "s2")@1;
wanted("n", "pen")@1;
